   118	
   119	## 7. Names
   120	
   121	**PASS — no owner-supplied name is needed.** All named people and places in chapters 1–6 already exist in the plan or inherited canon: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Teague, Pike, Hesk, Vell, Ephram, Reydan, Daeva, Lowmarch, Thornwater, Ostrand, Ternhall, Denvash, Ardenmere, the Fallow, Stair, and Hall (`BOOK_MAP.md:19-29,480-484`; `manuscript/chapter-01.md:15-19,49-65`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:295-301`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:87-93`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:245-253`). The factor, ferryman, ferryman's boy, ice carter, keeper, older healer, tall one, broad man/bow, young one, bowman, steading's woman, and three grey men remain unnamed roles (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:3-45,197-251`; `manuscript/chapter-02.md:15-47`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:81-85,169`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:61-77`). No animal receives a name.
   122	
   123	## 8. Next-movement inheritance not already carried by Packet 002
   124	
   125	Packet 002 already carries day 270, the six, Oryn's first post-thaw stop, Lira's two uncertain arms, Brom's bound/unread shoulder, the one-week ferry prediction, and Karis's unanswered case (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:18-20`). Its author must additionally inherit:
   126	
   127	- **Cael and the fragments:** deployment is 29, not 27; the calf and river-ice reads are the two counted additions. Shadow remains exactly twice and sealed; Anchor's counted uses remain two; Tide was refused and unused; the still place remains untouched (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:225-229`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:239-243`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:211-217`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:189-201`). His near sight recovered after both read bills, and his day-140 knuckles are old minor damage by day 270 (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:217-225`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:191-209`).
   128	- **The anomaly:** the cord reads forty-two strides in four hands and forty-one and a piece in Cael's, three times; Ternhall is a hair short and Hesk a hair long only in his hand; the tools are sound; Karis has preserved one hair; ruling `hold`; no cause or inference (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:3-155,259`). Oryn knows these facts and has offered no theory (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:189-201`).
   129	- **Cord definition:** after fixes, one full kit cord is twenty strides, four knots at five-stride intervals; the ash slip takes leftover strides (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:9-13,25-49`; fixes 3–7).
   130	- **Lira:** her right ankle is newly mended; she walks on the ball of it and wears the oversized carter boot without its old stuffing. Her left arm is released but slow for a month, aches in wet for a year, and is not to be fallen on (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127-151`). She still has Oryn's crossbow, hook, and one bolt; no return occurs (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:7`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:283`).
   131	- **Brom:** the right shoulder remains in the older healer's four-yard drover's knot. Oryn declined to undo another healer's work and will inspect it beside her (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:139-143`). His hook was used on the ice rescue but remains with the crossbow kit (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:139-153`).
   132	- **Karis:** fifty-two sheets, map, two straightedges, kit, opened field ledger, one stored hair, and the eleven-line case remain under her control. She cannot read the four-sign index or know it is a grade; she has entered no causal theory (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:253-281`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:145-195`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:227-253`). After fix 14, *west* has now been spoken once at the day-268 table.
   133	- **Seln:** his locked case remains shut; he taught nobody; he has begun a second hazel wand and reaches forty notches on day 270; he already recognized Treswick/Deepstacks when Karis said them (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:247,253,283`). He still does not explain the rival clock.
   134	- **Oryn:** she knows the fourth-site description, the map line, and the instrument anomaly, but has not read Cael and will not until she knows the purpose (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:163-209`). She did not take the sixth chair (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:223-225`). Her grey jenny remains at Thornwater; the brown mule is with the six at Lowmarch (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:131-147`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:65-77,217`).
   135	- **Teague's five:** they remain at the upper inn; the wrist is bound under the older healer's no-Force order, the after-thaw term stands, the silent-yard relationship exists, and Teague is entered as the better captain (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:157-223`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:219-231`). Apply the forward rulings that the spear is a man and Teague can read (§2.1–2.2).
   136	- **Money, board, debts, and letters:** 118 living marks; sealed reserve untouched; eleven completed Pike lines; cloth still eleventh; sixty yards of four-strand rope owed for the first boat; one reed hurdle owed; Ephram's letter still due on the first boat; mule's cold-term shed fee paid (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:271`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:295-299`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:215-219,281-283`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:75-91`).
   137	- **Fourth site and knowledge perimeter:** still unentered, unnamed, and untested; no sheet; no theory; nobody outside the six knows the mechanism, the instrument anomaly, or Karis's case (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:163-201,227-275`). The Compact response cannot have crossed the shut river before the day-277 ferry (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:99-103`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:233-241`).
