    34	- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
    35	- **The reveal is delivered once, in the record's voice:** the leaf in the Deepstacks. "The Architect" is the record's title; the name is scraped away; it was about four hundred years ago; the purpose was "that the un-bound should not come again". The chronicle's "went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" is **marked, not read**.
    36	- **Five sites lie on one bearing, ages ascending east.** The court is the fifth and the oldest, about 1,107 yards across, and the end of the line. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 5] It is **unnamed** ("the court", lowercase). The taxonomy is decoded: a stroke alone, a stroke and bar, a stroke and two bars.
    37	- **Karis's lamps finding** is stated and filed unexplained, on a page separate from the leaf, with no line drawn between them.
    38	- **The crack:** a directive and a filed objection under two seals that Vastin could name and does not.
    39	- **Vastin** is on the stick until the thirtieth day of Oryn's treatment month [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] ("Thirty's the month"). He walks with the five **unadmitted**. He has not asked to join and nobody has asked him.
    40	- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
    41	- **Teague** turns west with three practitioners and the healer of no Path. **The young one is dead**, buried under stone at the pass's east mouth. His name was said once by the broad man and is never written. [OWNER-pending #54] Teague carries Cael's letter to Hesk. "After the next thaw. Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
    42	- **The faceless faction** has reached three times (the alley, the Span's watch, the pass) and broken each time. It is unnamed, unlocated and faceless.
    43	- **Count at the rim:** "Six. Six and no mule." That is Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Vastin. The word is "West."
    44	- **Body ledger at close:** Brom's forearm is bound (bolt, pass) and he has a week of colours. Karis's left hand is bound and will scar ("It'll leave a line"). The broad man's leg is knit and his shoulder bound. Teague's arm faces a splint warning. Vastin is on day 29 of 30. Cael's ribs "will carry. They'll hurt."
    45	- **Cleon** stays under Treswick with the leaf and the board: "Work. Not a finding."
