   183	The source's Book 8 makes Teague's spear-carrier a tall woman throughout. The edition's locked Book 7 wrote this unnamed person as a man in five places (ch25:85 "a man with a spear"; ch51:357; ch52:45, :335, :337), because Book 7's plan never gave a gender and nobody caught it against Book 8. Book 8's protected text (§10) contains no gendered reference to the spear, and Book 8 Movement 1 uses no pronoun.
   184	**Default in force: Book 8 follows the locked Book 7 — a tall man** — as the edition followed its own earlier books in #1 (Pellin) and #7 (Bracken). No locked text changes and no protected text changes.
