editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-32-- **The silent yard** (two or three bouts across the cold term, ~1,500 each) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19]. Teague's crew and the five spar in the frozen meadow with steel and bodies, and no Paths. Cael loses to the tall woman's spear reach, then makes a visible correction. She never says a word to any of the five. Lira coaches from the bench, one-armed. The rival clock appears on the page. Teague is the better field captain.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-33-- **Cael's working inventory** (~6,000, across private practice in the ferryman's shed or the meadow at night). Each of the ten has its cost: Wind's burst and the lock beat; Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" when spoken); the Iron read; Compression's frame; Ember, one point at a time, with its burn (used at the Ring and the Stair); [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] Shadow's idle draw and the seal; Storm, its lanes and their bills (ten / ten / twelve; four lanes laid in Book 7; untested past three in a row); [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] Anchor used both ways; Blade; Tide, self and contact, which he has run on himself three times; no outward use without an ask and explicit yes. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-34-- **The anomaly as a scene** (168th). Karis has everyone pace the yard with the cord. It reads forty-two for everyone and "forty-one and a piece" for him, three times. The edges read a hair short and a hair long in his hands. Her ruler sentence is said twice, first as a rule and then not as one. Log it verbatim: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-35-- **Karis's case grows in pieces** through the cold term. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19] She says the full sentence about west on the 263rd. The thaw comes, and the Thornwater road opens on the 264th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-36-- **Thornwater** (265th–266th). The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. "Five months and twenty days." [OWNER-pending #56] / "That's a season. Take it off." Oryn waits for Lira to undo the sling herself. "Will you mend it." / "Lie still": this is Lira's first ask since Norhold. The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole." The map on her table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "Neither do you. Write that down too." She will not read him yet. She comes down to Lowmarch, unasked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:37:- **Six at Lowmarch** (268th): 118 marks. Karis makes her case, and **Treswick and the Deepstacks are spoken for the first time**, along with the scholars' provision and "a man there who is". Oryn's reservation about the station goes unsaid. **The closing log (270th), verbatim.**
