editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-45-- Cael is nineteen, with no birthday. He has ten fragments; the still place is not read or touched. **Oryn does not read Cael** (§13). Lira asks nobody for anything before Thornwater. **Seln teaches nobody.** The tall woman, the broad man and the older healer do not speak to the five. Teague's crew stays unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:46:- There is no Iron Wall and no Vastin in this movement. Vastin is still inside the Compact, and nothing hints otherwise. No Force is shown in Cael's presence. No silent-yard bout drills a wall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:47:- Karis cannot read the index, and does not know that it is a grade. She does not name Cleon to anyone. "Treswick" is first said at the 268th table.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-48-- The anomaly is deniable and gets no theory. Nobody says *who* or *why* about the pattern.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-49-- **Invent no new numeric ceilings for fragments. Preserve every numeric ceiling and bill fixed by canon.** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 19]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-50-- Reader Standard. Audio-first referents: with five people and Teague's four unnamed, attribute every line by action or name.
