editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md-17-> - **The anomaly:** the cord reads forty-two strides in four hands and forty-one and a piece in Cael's, three times; Ternhall is a hair short and Hesk a hair long only in his hand; the tools are sound; Karis has preserved one hair; ruling `hold`; no cause or inference (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:3-155,259`). Oryn knows these facts and has offered no theory (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:189-201`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md-18-> - **Cord definition:** after fixes, one full kit cord is twenty strides, four knots at five-stride intervals; the ash slip takes leftover strides (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:9-13,25-49`; fixes 3–7).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md-19-> - **Lira:** her right ankle is newly mended; she walks on the ball of it and wears the oversized carter boot without its old stuffing. Her left arm is released but slow for a month, aches in wet for a year, and is not to be fallen on (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127-151`). She still has Oryn's crossbow, hook, and one bolt; no return occurs (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:7`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:283`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md-20-> - **Brom:** the right shoulder remains in the older healer's four-yard drover's knot. Oryn declined to undo another healer's work and will inspect it beside her (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:139-143`). His hook was used on the ice rescue but remains with the crossbow kit (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:139-153`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md-21-> - **Karis:** fifty-two sheets, map, two straightedges, kit, opened field ledger, one stored hair, and the eleven-line case remain under her control. She cannot read the four-sign index or know it is a grade; she has entered no causal theory (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:253-281`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:145-195`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:227-253`). After fix 14, *west* has now been spoken once at the day-268 table.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:22:> - **Seln:** his locked case remains shut; he taught nobody; he has begun a second hazel wand and reaches forty notches on day 270; he already recognized Treswick/Deepstacks when Karis said them (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:247,253,283`). He still does not explain the rival clock.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md-23-> - **Oryn:** she knows the fourth-site description, the map line, and the instrument anomaly, but has not read Cael and will not until she knows the purpose (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:163-209`). She did not take the sixth chair (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:223-225`). Her grey jenny remains at Thornwater; the brown mule is with the six at Lowmarch (`book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:131-147`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:65-77,217`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md-24-> - **Teague's five:** they remain at the upper inn; the wrist is bound under the older healer's no-Force order, the after-thaw term stands, the silent-yard relationship exists, and Teague is entered as the better captain (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:157-223`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:219-231`). Apply the forward rulings that the spear is a man and Teague can read (§2.1–2.2).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md-25-> - **Money, board, debts, and letters:** 118 living marks; sealed reserve untouched; eleven completed Pike lines; cloth still eleventh; sixty yards of four-strand rope owed for the first boat; one reed hurdle owed; Ephram's letter still due on the first boat; mule's cold-term shed fee paid (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:271`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:295-299`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:215-219,281-283`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:75-91`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md-26-> - **Fourth site and knowledge perimeter:** still unentered, unnamed, and untested; no sheet; no theory; nobody outside the six knows the mechanism, the instrument anomaly, or Karis's case (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:163-201,227-275`). The Compact response cannot have crossed the shut river before the day-277 ferry (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:99-103`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:233-241`).
