editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-142-| **Lira** | To find out what she is without a ladder | Asks Oryn to mend the ankle (her first ask since Norhold). Fights on through the arm's first warning (M2), then listens at the second. Keeps her registry paper in her coat and goes up as a hand. Looks at the whole ladder and it does not pull. Holds her question at the court ("Well?") and accepts "on the road". | 12 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:143:| **Brom** | Worth without a number | Prices Vastin at three hundred miles. Takes the cart's weight on the good shoulder and pays for it. Declines the broker's post by picking up the box. Says "Good" to Cleon. Carries at Teague's leave. | 10 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:144:| **Karis** | To be right and believed, with a primary source | Learns the kit. Makes the case for west. Owns the response to Vastin's flat. Reads the leaf once and asks that nobody say it back. Keeps two pages at a spring, a hole and a fire. Sits with Vastin after the pass. | 14 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:145:| **Seln** | To keep his old life undecided and his own | Tells only Brom about the posts. Sets the sheet before Cael without a word. Teaches Vastin the first thing he ever teaches anyone. Truthful deflection at the yard door. Walks the tiers and decides nothing. Keeps the cache "a while longer". Climbs the swept scree. | 10 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-146-| **Oryn** | The route; to be nobody's recruit | Releases the arm only when Lira lifts the sling herself. Comes to Lowmarch unasked. Sets the station term in the log. Routes north. Rejoins as a stop. Asks every time. Walks on east at the cairn. Will not hear the leaf at her table. Turns north "the day I have to". | 11 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:147:| **Vastin** | To dig one thing up before he's done; to learn to navigate without authority | Walks three hundred miles alone. Carries the case unasked. Consents to be counted as a hand. Holds the wall with nothing behind it. Asks for the wall to be entered. Does not name the seals. Takes Oryn's order. Does not ask to join. | 14 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:148:| **Cleon** | The work finished and believed, without leaving the Deepstacks | Sets terms at noon. Shows the inside of the Path to no one before Karis. Refuses to finish the sentence. Looks away from the boy deliberately. Comes up the stair once. | 6 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-149-| **Teague** | To be at the front of the thing; to keep his people | Holds the after-thaw term. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Names the contract's terms. Goes through the middle. Does not turn when the broad man falls. Does not put his three across the court's line. Carries the letter. | 7 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:150:| **Pike** | An honest ledger | Prices the cold term. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Prices Vastin at nothing yet. Leaves the season line blank, then dates it. | 4 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-151-| **The young one** (Teague's; unnamed; his name is never written) [OWNER-pending #54] | To be counted as crew, not the boy with the cloth | Carries the cloth. Volunteers at the seep and is stopped. Steps over the iron when Teague looks at him ("Four"). Nods with his whole head. Goes to the broad man. | 5 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-152-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-153-The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59], the broad man and the older healer get two or three beats each, inside Teague's arc. **Keep every member of Teague's crew unnamed** (canon: "keep unnamed unless a later card needs one"; never invent a name for an existing role).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-154-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-155-### E. New episodes inside canon (≈23,000; most are counted under A above)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-156-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:157:The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-158-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-159-### F. Humour and warmth (≈12,000, distributed; no quota)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-160-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:161:Each person keeps their own comic habit. Brom says "It's a boot" and gives one-word essays ("They shoe by the tier"). Pike speaks ledger. Oryn: "Everybody says that now" and "I'm going to have to find another word". Lira finds an essay in a single word. "Noted" spreads through the cast like a borrowed tool, in the sequence locked in §13. Running jokes: the mule's empty chair; the mule as the only one of twelve who never knows what happened; the ferryman watching people use his river; Vastin's good manners from a man "served all his life and never once fed". When pain is in the room, humour stops performing.
