editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-347-### Tier A — canon-quoted and system text
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-348-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-349-1. **The leaf (S15):** "In the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land and no wall stood against them and no law held, and the cities of the east were emptied and the cities of the west were emptied and the rivers ran wrong" … "there came one who saw the shape of it, and set himself to the ordering. And he made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling, that each should know what he is and none should be what he is not. And he set the apparatus over all the land, and the land was ordered, and the un-bound came no more." / "And the" [the scraped name: four or five letters' width, the first upright stroke showing] "— set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it. And this is the reason of the apparatus, and this is all of its reason, and let none who come after forget it, though the un-bound be forgotten: that they should not come again."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-350-2. **The chronicle (S15):** "— and of him it is said that he did not die in the way of men, but went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" [a thumb's width of hole]. Karis: "Marked." Cleon: "Marked."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-351-3. **Karis's copy and finding (S15):** "and the" [gap drawn] "set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it." / *Older. Made. Us.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:352:4. **Vastin's page (S3):** "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-353-5. **The technician's sheet (S3):** "Deep layer. Sequence initiated" [a Compact date] "Unreadable. Not halted. Running. Correlated with classification event —" [brush bar]. Karis's note: *not read*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-354-6. **The surveyor's remark (S5):** "Behaves as device. Cannot be."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:355:7. **Directive and objection (S20):** "Findings under the fifth column to be held. Not for onward transmission. Not for citation. Not for the seat." / "Objection entered: the holding of a finding is not the finding's disproof. Refer to the seat." / Vastin: "Somebody wanted this buried. Somebody else put it in writing that it shouldn't be. That's not a monolith. That's a crack."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-356-8. **The lamps finding (S20):** "They fail the way a hundred lamps fail when one wire's cut. Not the way a hundred souls fall silent."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-357-9. **Cleon's limit (S11):** "I can tell you these are orders. I can't tell you what they order. For that you need the language, and the language is in the text, not the stone. That's her work, not mine." And: "It doesn't work on a river, and it doesn't work on a man, and it doesn't work on a tree, because nobody chose where the branches went. It costs me my eyes for an hour after and nothing else."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-358-10. **Cleon's warning (S13):** "I'm going to pretend you didn't tell me that," he said, "for your sake, not mine. But I'll tell you one thing for free, since you can apparently take my whole trade by watching me work it for a minute." … "Everything I read is *made*. Stone, ink, seal — somebody built it, so I can see how. If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — " He stopped. "Don't tell me. Don't tell anyone. Just remember I said it." Chapter-close sentence: "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-359-11. **Cleon's goodbye (S17):** "Work. Not a finding." / "Mind the stair. It leans."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:360:12. **Fragment eleven (S12):** "Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-361-13. **Fragment twelve (S13):** "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth." Then: *He looked away. Kept.* *Not a man.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-362-14. **Fragment thirteen (S19):** "Force-adjacent. Teague. Partial. Bronze. Impulse along the line of the frame at contact: from the ground, through the man, out at the hand, and nothing to either side of the line. Needs a thing to push against — the barricade, the ground under the feet; nothing at a distance; nothing from the air. A body's length. The cost back along the same line, every time, at the place the line comes out. Engagement field: close; braced. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Thirteenth."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-363-(Notice typography follows the edition's convention for system text. The notices must read aloud as prose.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-364-15. **Hesk's dividers note (S14):** "A rule says a line is true. A divider says how far, and carries it. You've the first. Here's the second, and mind the points; they'll go through a thumb as easy as a sheet. Lines are for finding out how far a thing is from another thing. Everything is. — H."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-365-16. **The grade (S17):** "A mark is a grade. The one they give a boy at fourteen says what he's *for*." … "The one on a sheet says how *old* the thing is." / "Somebody laid them down in order" / "It's observation. I'm telling you what the paper says. Not what it means." / Teague: "Oldest last." … "Then that's where we're going."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-366-17. **Pole two (S16):** Lira: "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Cael: "Since my Kindling I thought the system forgot to make room for me," … "It didn't forget. It was *built* so there'd be no room. Four hundred years of a whole world, so that I wouldn't happen." … "I happened anyway." / Lira: "Yeah." … "Now what." / Cael: "Now we find out how old the oldest one is. Karis has a bearing and the marks, and the records to read them against. There's a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine." … "I want to stand in the middle of it." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:367:18. **Vastin at the fire (S16):** "I believed it was imperfect." … "Now you're telling me it was *aimed*." … "At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." / Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I did." / "His?" / "No. I read it, after. I did not sign it." … "I would have." / "Yes," Lira said. "You would have."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-368-19. **Ribs (S22):** "That's a line," she said. "That's not yours." / "It's mine now."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-369-20. **Teague's lesson (S21):** "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:370:21. **The court (S23–24):** Vastin: "I stood at a line for forty years," Vastin said, "and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it." … "This is where they drew it." / Karis: "It's the first one." / Lira: "Right." / Oryn: "Nothing," … "Everything, round it." … "Same as you." / Teague: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough." … "Field's mine. This isn't field." / at the centre: "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-371-22. **Departures (S24):** Teague: "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." / Oryn: "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." / Seln: "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." / "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. / "Twenty-nine tomorrow," / "Thirty's the month," [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:372:23. **Pike (S2; S17):** "What'd he do?" / "Nothing," Vastin said. "Out here. Nothing yet." / "Then he's nothing yet." And the 297th line: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:373:24. **Vastin's papers (S8):** "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once, so that nobody asks twice."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-374-25. **Oryn at Millrace (S18):** "There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow*. I've spent my life reading flow. Whatever that is, it's not the kind of thing my Path was built for." / "Then it's not mine." … "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." … "Lie still when I say. That's still the term." / "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-375-26. **The rate (S19 log):** "Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md-376-27. **The contract (S17):** "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall." / Force: "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice."
