+
+### Standing constraints
+
+**PARTIAL.** All standing constraints hold except one phrase at `chapter-03.md:167`: “he had put his Path through a thing.” It is authorial narration and violates the brief's explicit “never ‘his Path’ in your own prose,” even though the Path belongs to Teague rather than Cael. Line fix 1 changes only that label and leaves the cost/accounting beat intact.
+
+The OWNER-pending #56 unit, “Five months and twenty days.”, occurs once at `chapter-06.md:89`, verbatim and unglossed. The tall spear remains pronoun-free, consistent with OWNER-pending #59; Teague is never said to be unable to read. The movement is season-blind, uses no English month or weekday, gives no numerical years-since-Kindling count, and mints no names.
