books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-17.md:117:Force. He had the card for it from a marsh and the thing itself now, and they agreed. Not a Path a man carried in his body, as Iron went, or set in front of it, as a wall. A Path that went *through* him: impulse, at the moment of contact, along the line of the frame from the ground to the hand, and nothing to the side of the line, and nothing at a distance, and nothing at all without a thing to push against. And the cost came back along the same line it had gone out on. The wrist clicked because the wrist was where the line came out, and the man had a boy with a cloth, and that was all of Force at Bronze in one cart in one meadow.

